# E00 MultipleMessages: parallel, and each worker sends its request to another worker drawn at random, so names and
# order vary; compared: who is started, who reports, the counts of requests and replies, one request per worker, and
# the manager printing "reporting" right after each report. In legacy (X1, D89) the replies are never handled: no
# "replying".
cover all
fact start ^\[Manager -> (Worker\d)\]: start$
fact report ^\[(Worker\d) -> Manager\]: report$
fact reporting ^\t\[Manager\]: (Worker\d) reporting$
fact request ^\[(Worker\d) -> (Worker\d)\]: request$
fact reply ^\[(Worker\d) -> (Worker\d)\]: reply$
fact replying ^\t\[Manager\]: (Worker\d) replying$
fact manager ^(?:\[Worker\d -> Manager\]: (report)|\t\[Manager\]: Worker\d (reporting))$
optional replying
same start bag
same report bag
same reporting bag
same request count
same reply count
same manager seq
check request count == 5
check request distinct(0) == 5
check reply count == 5
check replying count == 0
fact error (Exception|out of range)
optional error
check error count == 0
